{"type":"standard","title":"Christina Bohannan","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Christina Bohannan</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q106588848","titles":{"canonical":"Christina_Bohannan","normalized":"Christina Bohannan","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Christina Bohannan</span></span>"},"pageid":67466458,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/ChristinaBohannan.jpg/330px-ChristinaBohannan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":462},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/ChristinaBohannan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2918,"height":4085},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1367897186","tid":"23b99688-9112-11f1-b25b-1d6610553dc8","timestamp":"2026-08-05T21:10:52Z","description":"American politician, legal scholar and engineer (born 1971)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Bohannan","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Bohannan?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Bohannan?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Christina_Bohannan"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Bohannan","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Christina_Bohannan","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Bohannan?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Christina_Bohannan"}},"extract":"Christina Bohannan is an American politician and law professor who served as the Iowa State Representative for the 85th district from 2021 to 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, she was elected in 2020, succeeding Vicki Lensing who served ten terms in the Iowa House of Representatives.","extract_html":"<p><b>Christina Bohannan</b> is an American politician and law professor who served as the Iowa State Representative for the 85th district from 2021 to 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, she was elected in 2020, succeeding Vicki Lensing who served ten terms in the Iowa House of Representatives.</p>"}